.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-DOCTOR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-doctor
.Nd check a kldload host against what its install should be, and say how to fix each difference
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs a fixed list of checks against the machine it is on and prints one
JSON document on standard output: a result for every check, grouped two
ways, and a count of each outcome.
It changes nothing on the machine except its own log.
.Pp
Each check has one of four outcomes:
.Bl -tag -width "skip"
.It Li ok
The thing checked is as a kldload install leaves it.
.It Li warn
It is not, but the machine works; a warning names the difference and the
command that removes it.
.It Li fail
It is not, and something that should work does not.
.It Li skip
The check does not apply to this machine, or could not look.
A machine installed without Kubernetes skips every Kubernetes check; a
check that needs root, run as a user, skips and says
.Dq not checked -- run as root .
A skip is never counted as a pass.
.El
.Pp
Checks follow the install, not a single idea of a healthy machine: a
.Ql core
install, which ships no kldload tools, is not failed for their absence,
and Prometheus, Grafana and Ollama are judged only where the install put
them.
.Pp
It should run as root.
Run as a user, it cannot read
.Pa /root
or ask libvirt about the system's machines, and says so for each check
that needed to; the Kubernetes checks then use the user's own kubeconfig.
.Pp
A run takes about two seconds on a machine with no cluster.
With a cluster, the mesh check logs in to every node over
.Xr ssh 1 ,
which takes longer.
When the apiserver named by the kubeconfig does not answer its port within
1.5 seconds, every check that would ask it is skipped at once instead of
waiting out a timeout each.
.Pp
The web console's Doctor view,
.Xr kld 1
and the estate sweep's per-machine report run
.Nm
and read the same document.
.Ss Output
The document has four keys:
.Bl -tag -width "subsystems"
.It Li summary
The number of results with each outcome:
.Li ok , warn , fail , skip .
.It Li results
One object per check, in the order they ran, each with
.Li subsystem , name , status , expected , actual , severity
.Po
.Li critical , high , medium
or
.Li low
.Pc
and
.Li remediation ,
the command to run, or an empty string.
.It Li subsystems
The same objects, keyed by subsystem.
.It Li version
The document's format,
.Ql 1.0 .
.El
.Pp
Keys are sorted.
A check's name is the same whatever its outcome, so its history can be
found in the log by name.
.Ss The checks
In the order they run, with checks of the same kind taken together.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li boot/bootfs set
The pool's
.Li bootfs
property names a boot environment.
Without it ZFSBootMenu has no default and an unattended reboot stops at
its menu.
Fails when unset.
.It Li desktop/audio sinks
PipeWire has at least one sink, asked as the user at the screen.
Skips with no
.Xr pactl 1
or nobody seated.
.It Li desktop/dock pins
At least one kldload launcher or console is pinned in the GNOME dock of
the user at the screen, or, with nobody seated, in the system default.
Fails when none is; that is how an interrupted first boot shows.
.It Li disk/AI payload reclaimed
The 3.3 GB AI payload under
.Pa /root/darksite/ollama
was removed after installing.
Warns when it is still there, unless
.Pa /etc/kldload/keep-darksite
exists.
.It Li containers/docker storage driver
Docker stores its layers on the
.Li zfs
driver, so they can be snapshotted and sent.
Fails on any other driver.
Skips with no Docker or no daemon.
.It Li zfs/rpool health
.Li rpool
is imported and ONLINE.
Fails otherwise, at critical severity.
.It Li zfs/pool errors
.Ql zpool status -x
reports every pool healthy.
Warns otherwise.
.It Li zfs/arc sized
The ARC holds less than 80% of memory.
Warns above.
.It Li zfs/sanoid timer
.Pa sanoid.timer ,
which takes the scheduled snapshots, is active.
Warns otherwise.
.It Li kldload-zfs/namespace exists
.Li rpool/kldload
and its
.Li secrets , state
and
.Li playbooks
datasets exist.
Warns for each missing one.
.It Li kldload-zfs/secrets encrypted
.Li rpool/kldload/secrets
is encrypted.
Fails when it is not.
.It Li network/wireguard module
The
.Li wireguard
kernel module is loaded.
Warns otherwise.
.It Li network/wireguard mesh
Lists the WireGuard interfaces; skips when there are none.
.It Li network/virbr0 up
libvirt's default bridge is administratively up.
A bridge with no machine attached has no carrier; that is reported, not
warned about.
Warns when it is down.
.It Li kubernetes/apiserver
The apiserver the kubeconfig names answers.
Fails on a control plane (one holding
.Pa /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml ) ;
elsewhere warns, since a kubeconfig left by a cluster that is gone is
common.
When it does not answer, every check from here to
.Li observability/metrics-server
skips.
.It Li kubernetes/nodes ready
Every registered node is Ready.
A node whose machine is powered off is named in
.Li expected .
Fails at critical severity.
.It Li kubernetes/cilium healthy , k8s-stack/cilium agents
A Ready Cilium agent on every node.
Fail when short.
.It Li k8s-stack/cilium operator , hubble relay , metallb , zfs csi
Every pod of each is Ready.
Fail when short.
.It Li k8s-stack/hubble ui
Every Hubble UI pod is Ready.
Warns when short.
.It Li k8s-stack/gateway api
The Gateway API resource definitions are installed.
.It Li helm/releases
Every Helm release is
.Li deployed
or
.Li superseded .
Fails naming the others.
.It Li observability/metrics-server
metrics-server is Ready and
.Ql kubectl top node
answers.
Fails when it is missing or not Ready; warns when Ready but not
answering.
.It Li observability/prometheus , grafana
The service is active, where it is installed.
Fail when stopped.
.It Li observability/prometheus scrape
Prometheus scrapes the host's node exporter, and on a machine with a
cluster the Cilium, Hubble and Tetragon jobs too, each with at least one
target up.
Fails naming the missing or dark jobs.
.It Li observability/cilium scrape labels , tetragon scrape , hubble scrape
Each job's metrics arrive, with the labels the stock Cilium dashboards
filter by.
Skip while a job has not been scraped yet, which on a new cluster lasts
minutes; fail once it has and the data is still absent.
.It Li observability/grafana dashboards
No provisioned dashboard carries an unresolved
.Ql ${DS_PROMETHEUS}
placeholder, which leaves every panel empty.
.It Li observability/cluster firewall
Where an nftables policy drops traffic, the node subnet or the kubelet
port, and the pod network, are allowed in.
Skips where nothing drops.
.It Li kubernetes/cluster mesh peers
Every running cluster node
.Po
a machine named
.Ql kldload-cp*
or
.Ql kldload-w*
.Pc
holds a WireGuard peer for each other node and for this host, asked over
.Xr ssh 1 .
Fails on any difference, and on any node it could not reach.
.It Li k8s-stack/darksite charts , darksite images
The Helm charts and container images a cluster is deployed from without a
network are on the machine.
Skip on an install that carries no darksite.
.It Li ai/ollama
Ollama answers and has a model in memory.
Skips where Ollama is not installed; fails when it does not answer.
kldload keeps models loaded
.Pq Ev OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE Ns =-1 ,
so an empty memory is a warning: the first prompt waits for a load.
.It Li ai/webui tools
The web console still offers the assistant its eight observability tools.
.It Li installer/artifacts
The files an install puts in place for the automatic deployment and the
cluster tools are there.
Skips on
.Ql core .
.It Li services/kldload-webui
The web console's service is active.
.It Li services/libvirt
.Xr virsh 1
connects to
.Li qemu:///system ,
whichever of the modular daemons or
.Xr libvirtd 8
this host runs.
.It Li services/cli tools
.Xr kvm-create 8 ,
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr kldload-db 8 ,
.Xr kldload-inventory 8 ,
.Nm
and
.Xr kexport 8
are on the path.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
Runs no check and needs no root.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KUBECONFIG
The cluster the Kubernetes checks ask, as for
.Xr kubectl 1 ;
unset, root's is
.Pa /root/.kube/config .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/kldload-doctor.log
A line per run with its counts, and a line per warning and failure.
Moved to
.Pa /root/kldload-doctor.log.old
past 2 MB.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/profile
The install's profile; on
.Ql core
the artifacts check skips.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/keep-darksite
Present on a machine kept as a mirror: the AI payload is kept on purpose.
.It Pa /root/darksite/
The offline payload the darksite checks look in.
.It Pa /var/lib/grafana/dashboards/
The dashboards the Grafana check reads.
.It Pa /etc/nftables.conf
The firewall the cluster firewall check reads, when a drop policy is in
effect.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
No check failed.
Warnings and skips do not change this.
.It 1
At least one check failed.
.It 2
A check crashed; it is reported as a failure of subsystem
.Li runner ,
named for its function.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Every output below was printed by
.Nm
on a kldload desktop with no cluster on 2026-09-29.
.Ss Usage (-h, --help)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-doctor --help
usage: kldload-doctor

Profiles this host against a known-good baseline and prints JSON on stdout:
  .summary            counts of ok / warn / fail / skip
  .results[]          one per check: subsystem, name, status, actual,
                      expected, severity and the remediation command
There are no options. Read it with jq, for example the checks that are not ok:

  kldload-doctor | jq -r '.results[] | select(.status!="ok")
      | "\e(.status)\et\e(.name)\et\e(.remediation)"'

Each run is also appended to /root/kldload-doctor.log (fails and warns).

Exit status: 0 no check failed, 1 at least one failed, 2 a check crashed.
See kldload-doctor(8).
.Ed
.Ss The verdict
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-doctor | jq .summary
{
  "fail": 0,
  "ok": 21,
  "skip": 21,
  "warn": 1
}
# kldload-doctor >/dev/null; echo $?
0
.Ed
.Ss What needs attention
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-doctor | jq -r '.results[] | select(.status=="warn" or .status=="fail") | "\e(.status)\et\e(.subsystem)/\e(.name)\et\e(.actual)"'
warn	ai/ollama	no models loaded -- the first prompt will wait for one to load
.Ed
.Ss One check in full
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-doctor | jq '.results[] | select(.name=="virbr0 up")'
{
  "actual": "up, no carrier (no guest attached)",
  "expected": "administratively UP",
  "name": "virbr0 up",
  "remediation": "",
  "severity": "medium",
  "status": "ok",
  "subsystem": "network"
}
.Ed
.Ss By subsystem
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-doctor | jq -r '.subsystems | to_entries[] | "\e(.key)\et\e(.value | map(.status) | join(" "))"'
ai	warn ok
boot	ok
containers	skip
desktop	skip ok
disk	ok
helm	skip
installer	ok
k8s-stack	skip skip skip skip skip skip skip ok skip
kldload-zfs	ok ok
kubernetes	skip skip skip skip
network	ok skip ok
observability	skip ok ok skip skip skip ok ok skip
services	ok ok ok
zfs	ok ok ok ok
.Ed
.Ss The log
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# tail -2 /root/kldload-doctor.log
# ts=2026-09-29T22:43:04.158389 ok=21 fail=0 warn=1 skip=21
  [WARN] ai/ollama: no models loaded -- the first prompt will wait for one to load
.Ed
.Ss As a user
The checks that read
.Pa /root
or ask the system libvirt say they did not look, the Kubernetes checks ask
the user's own kubeconfig (here one left by a cluster that is gone), and
the log cannot be written; the verdict is still printed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-doctor | jq -c .summary
kldload-doctor: run not logged: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/root/kldload-doctor.log'
{"fail":0,"ok":18,"skip":22,"warn":3}
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "kldload-doctor: run not logged: REASON"
The log could not be written: a run as a user, or a read-only
.Pa /root .
The document and the exit status are unaffected.
.It "crashed: MESSAGE"
In a result of subsystem
.Li runner :
the named check raised an error instead of returning a result.
The run carries on with the others and exits 2.
.It "not checked -- run as root"
The check needs to read
.Pa /root
or ask the system libvirt; its skip means nothing about the machine.
.It "apiserver unreachable (port probe)"
Seen in the
.Li actual
of a Kubernetes check: see
.Li kubernetes/apiserver
above.
.El
