.Sh HISTORY
Most checks carry a date: the defect they were written to catch, or a
false alarm of their own that was taken out.
Two that shaped the rest:
on 2026-08-19 the nodes check had been taught to expect powered-off nodes,
and stayed green while an etcd member, an apiserver and a scheduler were
down; every registered node is expected Ready since.
The libvirt check once reported a healthy host running the modular
daemons as broken and prescribed enabling
.Xr libvirtd 8 ,
the command that, on 2026-09-16, had pushed those daemons' sockets out and
cost a six-node cluster and fifteen golden images; it asks
.Xr virsh 1
since, and prescribes by what the host runs.
.Pp
On 2026-09-29, writing this page: the metrics-server check failed every
machine without a cluster, so each exited 1; the bridge check and the dock
check could not fail, one matching
.Ql UP
in the list of a down link's flags, the other counting GNOME's own default
pins; an apiserver that did not answer skipped every Kubernetes check
without saying so; run as a user, the darksite checks reported an absent
darksite and a reclaimed payload they had not looked at; and four checks
changed name with their outcome.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
A pass means the checks passed, not that the machine is sound: nothing
here reads a disk's SMART data, tries a backup restore, or boots a
snapshot.
.Pp
The cluster checks know the Cilium, Hubble, MetalLB, ZFS CSI and Tetragon
that
.Xr kube-cluster 8
deploys; a cluster built otherwise skips or fails them by its labels, not
its health.
.Pp
The cluster firewall check reads
.Pa /etc/nftables.conf
for the pod network
.Li 10.244.0.0/16 ;
a cluster given another pod range by the network plan is warned about
until this check reads the plan.
